                <pb facs="0367" n="285" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg285"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 838.00/609.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the American
                    Minister.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-08-02T13:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 2,
                                1911—1 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Knox instructs Mr. Furniss in reply to his August 1, 1 and 3 p.m., that he
                    may accord temporary refuge to President Simon in the legation if necessary to
                    save innocent human life.</p>
            </div>
